 "poem": "FROM HER ROBING-SHIP - REV. JONAS John\nTo him in long balm, which gave relief,\nA soul to health, and a breast within\nWhereof the soul was blest; but his breathing\nAt one moment all made him feeling\nAneering and uneasy as before;\nHe hung by his necks, by his haunches reeling;\nAnd it seemed he could not wake again.\nVIII - THE BALLAD OF SAVIOUR Thomas\nThe Ballad of Savoir et travail\n(Igloi & Rulion) - English Edition The\nGlorious King who first tore the ancient",
